    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a concentrated focus on high-efficiency output, as our roster depth is pressured by the necessity of staying above the 40.0-point floor. **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable anchor today, checking in with a score of 62.45. Despite a slight downward adjustment for facing the southpaw Drohan, **Kyle Tucker**\u2019s elite base projection and favorable presence in the #5 hole make him an automatic start. While **Andy Pages** also makes the cut at 51.43, he sits in the marginal tier; his lower score is primarily a byproduct of hitting in the #8 spot against Drohan, which significantly caps his RBI potential compared to the top-of-order producers like **Gunnar Henderson** or **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Liam Hicks**, who flirted with the starting threshold at 39.61. While the optimizer appreciated his platoon edge against Williams, the high-skill profile of the opposing arm (2.95 xERA) penalized his floor enough to keep him on the pine. Similarly, **Brayan Rocchio** was bypassed due to a combination of a challenging matchup against Jax and a bottom-of-the-order assignment that dragged his efficiency score down to 38.88. We are currently navigating these decisions without the services of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill**, whose absence continues to tighten our lineup flexibility, requiring us to rely on the underlying plate discipline metrics of our fringe starters to avoid burning game caps on sub-optimal performances.",
